  "worked_solution": "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta -{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20618x={cos}^{2}\u20614x-{sin}^{2}\u20614x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}\u20614x-{cos}^{2}\u20614x)\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cos}^{2}\u20614x-{sin}^{2}\u20614x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}\u20618x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}\u20618x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(8\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}\u20612\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}\u20610] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
